<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wilhelm Junker</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1840">1840</a>–<a href="/years/1892">1892</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wilhelm Junker was a Russian-born explorer of German descent who travelled widely in north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Between 1879 and 1886 he explored the Uele and Mbomou basins and the lands of the Zande and Mangbetu, staying with rulers such as Zemio. Cut off by the Mahdist rising, he returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> by way of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, and his travel account became a major source on the region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wilhelm-junker.jpg" alt="Wilhelm Junker" width="320" height="526" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wilhelm Junker (6 April 1840 - 13 February 1892) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wilhelm_Junker_001.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
